---
title: "Breadcrumbs"
description: "Shows where the current page sits in the site's hierarchy, as a list of links."
tags: [navigation, accessibility, css]
usage: |
  Put an ordered list of links inside a `<nav>` with the `breadcrumbs` class. The
  separators are drawn with CSS, so they are not read out.
accessibility: |
  - Label the `<nav>`, for example `aria-label="Breadcrumbs"`, so it can be told
    apart from other navigation landmarks.
  - Mark the link to the current page with `aria-current="page"`.
---
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<nav aria-label="Breadcrumbs" class="breadcrumbs">
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#">#1</a></li>
    <li><a href="#">#2</a></li>
    <li><a aria-current="page" href="#">#3</a></li>
  </ol>
</nav>
